  "data": {
    "title": "Connectivity Patterns During Music Listening: Evidence for Action-Based Processing in Musicians",
    "text": "Title: Connectivity Patterns During Music Listening: Evidence for Action-Based Processing in Musicians\n\nConnectivity Analyses\nFor functional connectivity analysis, networks were generated by calculating, for each participant, the Pearson correlation between the time series of all possible combinations of voxel pairs, yielding a cross-correlation matrix representing the strength of association between each voxel pair.\n\nSubsequently, each correlation matrix was thresholded to generate a binary adjacency matrix. Fixed average degree thresholding was used, expressed as S = log(N)/log(K). In the present study, thresholds of S = 2.5 and S = 4.0 were used.\n\nStarting from the adjacency matrices, we calculated the node degree and global efficiency for each participant. To increase statistical power, data obtained with individual stimuli were concatenated before evaluating node degree.\n\nCommunity Structure Analysis\nCommunity structure analysis was performed using the QCut algorithm, which optimizes the modularity measure. Ten runs were performed for each participant, and the partition yielding the highest modularity value was retained. Scaled inclusivity was used to determine the consistency of community structure across participants."
  },
